= Sir Keith Joseph

[? if con_in_government = 1 and industry_secretary == "Joseph" : Secretary of State for Industry. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 and industry_secretary != "Joseph" : A Cabinet minister without a department to run. ?][? if con_in_government = 0 : In charge of policy and research. ?] Co-founder of the Centre for Policy Studies, and the intellectual engine of the new Conservatism. He might have been leader himself, had his speeches been better judged.

- @lecture_tour
- @stepping_stones
- @back_management
- @root: Return

@lecture_tour
title: University lecture tour
subtitle: Raises public support for free-market economics; the dries grow stronger.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next Shadow Cabinet action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; economic_liberalism += 5; dry_strength += 4; wet_dissent += 3

Sir Keith lectures on campuses across the country, sometimes over the shouting of left-wing students. The arguments get reported, and some of them stick.

@stepping_stones
title: "Stepping Stones"
view-if: policy_union_reform = 0
subtitle: Adopts trade union reform at once, with a strategy to sell it.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next Shadow Cabinet action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; policy_union_reform = 1; dry_strength += 3; wet_dissent += 6; union_backlash += 2

Sir Keith champions the confidential "Stepping Stones" report: the unions are the obstacle to recovery, and a Conservative government has to say so openly. Jim Prior is appalled.

@back_management
title: Back management against the unions
view-if: con_in_government = 1
subtitle: Union power falls; expect a fight.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next Cabinet action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; union_power -= 8; strike_wave += 1; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent) if union_backlash >= 60

Sir Keith makes it clear that the government will back managers like Michael Edwardes at British Leyland, who sacked "Red Robbo", the Longbridge convenor, and faced down the walkout that followed.
